WEBVTT

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.020
KENGAN LIFE-OR-DEATH

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.770
FIST

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.540
KENGAN LIFE-OR-DEATH

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:12.440
Wow. This place is packed.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.080
<i>World leaders are here?</i>

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:23.160
KAZUO YAMASHITA
PRESIDENT, YAMASHITA CORP

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:58.240
KENGAN LIFE-OR-DEATH

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.450
A woman?

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:06.160
Her name is Sayaka Katahara.
She's the chairman's daughter.

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:08.210
KAEDE AKIYAMA
CHAIRMAN'S SECRETARY, NOGI GROUP

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:09.210
Is she?

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.170
Ladies and gentlemen,
thank you all for coming.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:13.960
SAYAKA KATAHARA
DAUGHTER OF METSUDO KATAHARA

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:20.140
And now, the Kengan Life-or-Death
Tournament will begin!

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.650
<i>Kengan matches produce</i>
<i>such a special kind of enthusiasm.</i>

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:39.450
<i>They're nothing like</i>
<i>other public martial arts matches.</i>

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:45.700
METSUDO KATAHARA,
KENGAN ASSOCIATION CHAIRMAN

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.290
It's heating up already!

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:51.210
<i>I have great hopes for this tournament.</i>

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:26.930
THE BATTLE BEGINS

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.610
COSMO IMAI
FIGHTER, NISHIHONJI SECURITY SERVICES

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:42.490
<i>When I was younger and</i>
<i>a little more of a rascal,</i>

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.700
<i>I was getting myself into fights</i>
<i>day in, day out.</i>

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:49.870
<i>Bring it on, assholes!</i>

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:55.080
<i>On that day,</i>
<i>I was at something of a disadvantage.</i>

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.210
<i>I was fighting against four yakuza.</i>

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:02.340
<i>They got serious,</i>
<i>even though I was just a kid.</i>

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.380
<i>But then,</i>
<i>just when I thought I was a goner...</i>

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.470
<i>a hero showed up.</i>

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:16.520
<i>This ordinary looking guy</i>
<i>burst onto the scene...</i>

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:21.650
<i>and knocked those yakuza down in no time.</i>

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:25.820
<i>It turned out...</i>

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:27.240
MITSUYO KUREISHI
MMA FIGHTER

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:31.200
<i>...he was a mixed martial artist, known</i>
<i>in Japan at that time as "The White Hope."</i>

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.160
<i>I saw you fighting.</i>

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:36.540
<i>You've got some balls, kid.</i>

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.460
<i>So... why don't you learn martial arts?</i>

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:49.050
<i>His words changed my life dramatically.</i>

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:50.300
Hey.

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:54.310
AKIRA NISHIHONJI
PRESIDENT, NISHIHONJI SECURITY

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:55.430
How's it going?

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:57.350
Perfect.

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:00.230
This might be the best condition
I've ever been in.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:02.570
Hey, Cos.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.280
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:08.660
When you think you
don't stand a chance, just quit.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:11.160
Not that again.

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:13.080
I've told you a hundred times.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:17.460
You're my favorite junior,
you're more than just a fighter.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:22.790
Have you forgotten...
the sort of personality I have?

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:27.590
I hate losing more than anything.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.590
You're in good hands with me.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:34.100
I promise to take you
all the way through the championship.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:38.440
I knew you'd say that.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:40.520
Go win the battle.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:43.770
KENGAN LIFE-OR-DEATH

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:45.860
KENGAN MATCH

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:55.290
GAME ONE

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:58.410
<i>He's got an infinite desire for combat.</i>

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:03.460
He might be short, but he's strong enough
to take down any opponent he fights.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.460
<i>A young jujitsu master...</i>

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:10.470
<i>Can he add to the excitement</i>
<i>of the opening of the tournament?</i>

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:14.680
<i>Standing 171 cm tall and weighing 68 kg,</i>

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:18.930
<i>his kengan match record is</i>
<i>21 wins and no losses.</i>

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:25.480
He has amassed total assets
of 79 billion, 212 million yen.

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:29.400
Representing Nishihonji Security Services,

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:32.110
<i>also known as "The King of Stranglers,"</i>

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:36.030
<i>Cosmo Imai!</i>

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:51.630
All right. Let's get started.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:55.470
What the hell? He's just a little kid.

00:07:55.930 --> 00:07:58.060
Cosmo Imai, 19 years old.

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:00.180
He practices jujitsu.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:03.440
Despite his appearance,
he's won all 21 matches straight.

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:04.560
I mean...

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:06.520
RONALD HARAGUCHI
PRESIDENT, BOSS BURGER

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:08.320
...he's no match for you, though.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:11.650
Oh. Jujitsu?

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:15.490
I'll teach him his place,
he's just a cock sucker

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.660
who loves to use
ground grappling techniques.

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:19.330
ADAM DUDLEY
BOSS BURGER'S FIGHTER

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:21.290
VERSUS

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:27.340
<i>This man has beaten countless opponents.</i>

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:30.380
He'll take down anyone, armed or unarmed.

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:32.340
He's the Kingpin Brawler in Texas.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:37.300
<i>The violent thug from the land of the free</i>
<i>will go on a rampage on Ganryu Island.</i>

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:42.350
<i>Will he be the first foreign fighter ever</i>
<i>to win the Kengan Tournament championship?</i>

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:46.600
<i>Standing 192 cm tall</i>
<i>and weighing 107 kg,</i>

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:49.860
<i>his kengan match record</i>
<i>is one win and no losses.</i>

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:55.240
The total assets he has acquired
stand at seven billion, 646 million yen.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.870
Representing Boss Burger,

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:00.580
<i>also known as "The Emperor,"</i>

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:04.370
<i>Adam Dudley!</i>

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:21.890
<i>Look at them!</i>
<i>They're already glaring at each other.</i>

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:28.020
Hey, what kind of bullshit is this?
Do Japs make their bitches fight?

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:30.270
You've got a foul mouth.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:34.240
Well, it doesn't matter.
You won't be able to talk in a minute.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.660
<i>Well, well. They're raging.</i>

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:41.950
SHION SORYUIN
CHAIRWOMAN, KOUOU EDUCATION GROUP

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:44.000
What do you think of this match?

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:45.620
I really love cute guys and tough guys!

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:47.540
TOMOKO MATSUDA,
SECRETARY, KOUOU EDUCATION GROUP

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:50.040
That's not what I asked.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:53.710
Where did Kiryu go?

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:56.300
SETSUNA KIRYU
FIGHTER, KOUOU EDUCATION GROUP

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:02.720
The key to this match is how they bring
the fight to their field of expertise.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:04.520
SUEKICHI KANEDA
FIGHTER, GINOKUNIYA BOOKSHOP

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:07.640
That's true, seeing as their styles
are the complete opposite of each other.

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:09.310
NAOYA OHKUBO
FIGHTER, MUJI TV NETWORK

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:14.610
The big difference in physique
must surely work against Imai.

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:16.990
What do you think, Ohma?

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:22.080
Physique won't make a difference...

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:26.000
not to a fighting prodigy like Cosmo Imai.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:30.790
<i>Will the winner be the jujitsu master</i>
<i>of the Land of Rising Sun...</i>

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:35.260
<i>or the bullfighter from</i>
<i>the Land of the Free?</i>

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:38.720
Ready, get set!

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:43.510
<i>This is a face-off between two men</i>
<i>from opposite sides of the Pacific...</i>

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:47.060
with completely opposite fighting styles.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:51.310
<i>Which one of them will triumph?</i>

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:57.320
Fight!

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:03.950
It's on! The Kengan Life-or-Death
Tournament has finally begun!

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:21.010
<i>Shit! That was a heavy blow.</i>
<i>That didn't feel like a middleweight blow.</i>

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:24.260
<i>Great.</i>
<i>He seems perfectly prepared for this.</i>

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:28.220
<i>I'm used to fighting big guys.</i>

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:31.850
<i>I just need to make sure I avoid</i>
<i>getting hit from the front</i>

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:34.110
<i>and try to throw him off-balance.</i>

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:35.650
Quick little bitch.

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:45.240
He seems well prepared
for a heavyweight match.

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:48.620
<i>We don't mesh with each other.</i>

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:51.040
<i>Fine.</i>

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:54.330
<i>I'm going to force you to mesh with me!</i>

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:55.710
<i>Okay.</i>

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:57.880
<i>Your eyeballs are mine.</i>

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:02.880
Nice. A scissor throw!

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:04.340
Hell, yeah! He did it, Wakatsuki.

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:05.890
JUN SEKIBAYASHI
FIGHTER, GANDAI

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:07.260
Calm down, Seki. I saw it.

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:09.390
TAKESHI WAKATSUKI
FIGHTER, FURUMI PHARMA

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:10.520
He's got momentum.

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:13.690
From here on in,
they're in Imai's field of expertise.

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:15.980
<i>He has him pinned!</i>

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:18.570
Ground grappling techniques
are Imai's forte.

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:22.240
He's living up to the name of Cosmo
with these universe-class techniques.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.610
Is there anything Adam can do?

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:28.830
<i>That guy looks familiar for some reason.</i>

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:31.000
JERRY TYSON, 22ND CENTURY FAX'S FIGHTER
(ELIMINATED)

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:33.500
All right. I've scaled the mountain.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:36.330
This is over.

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:42.220
Who said it's over?

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:46.090
Save the speech
until you actually take me down.

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:53.480
Okay. That was my plan, anyway.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:56.270
From now on, I'm in charge.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:03.740
<i>Wow. This match is</i>
<i>starting to get pretty one-sided.</i>

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:07.280
<i>Imai's on the offensive,</i>
<i>showering Adam with blows.</i>

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:09.660
<i>Is it all over for Adam?</i>

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:12.830
<i>He's not letting his guard down.</i>

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:16.460
<i>I can't move onto a stranglehold.</i>

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:18.960
What's wrong, boy?

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:24.300
You couldn't even kill a mouse
with your pussy punches.

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:25.930
What?

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:37.400
Why did he dodge such a little jab?

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:40.860
<i>What's happened? Imai has dismounted.</i>

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:43.610
<i>Was he too concerned about</i>
<i>attacks coming from below?</i>

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:48.160
Why did he avoid that punch
when it wouldn't have done much damage?

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:52.410
You should've taken his arm at the moment
of impact and moved into the Arm Bar.

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:55.120
That was the right response.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.580
REI MIKAZUCHI AND RINO KURAYOSHI
OF GOLD PLEASURE GROUP

00:13:57.670 --> 00:14:00.460
If he hadn't dodged that blow,
this match could've been over.

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:01.500
Oh, really?

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:07.180
<i>He hardly touched me,</i>
<i>so why does it hurt this much?</i>

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:14.390
<i>What is going on?</i>

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:18.900
<i>Adam is getting back up</i>
<i>in a very unnatural way.</i>

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:21.230
<i>What the hell is his body made of?</i>

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:25.150
<i>His fighting spirit</i>
<i>has finally been ignited.</i>

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:29.070
<i>Now, Adam, show them your power.</i>

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:35.950
Sorry, boy.
We're back in my area of expertise.

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:44.590
That man is...

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:57.560
<i>Ice hockey is the only</i>
<i>modern sport in the world</i>

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:02.230
<i>where players are silently</i>
<i>authorized to hit each other.</i>

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:07.940
<i>However, the coefficient of friction</i>
<i>on an ice-rink is only 0.005.</i>

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:11.780
<i>In an environment where</i>
<i>you can barely keep your balance,</i>

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:14.910
<i>you can't throw powerful punches.</i>

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:16.290
<i>However...</i>

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:25.500
<i>Adam Dudley managed to deliver a large</i>
<i>number of knockouts on the rink.</i>

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:29.760
<i>The secret to his skill</i>
<i>was his well-built trunk.</i>

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:34.470
<i>Adam has an abnormally large</i>
<i>erector spinae muscle.</i>

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:37.390
<i>It greatly increases</i>
<i>the conductivity efficiency of force,</i>

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:43.310
<i>making his jabs powerful enough</i>
<i>to knock his opponents out cold.</i>

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:49.280
<i>Don't stop moving.</i>
<i>Shake him off with my speed...</i>

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:52.910
<i>until I take him down!</i>

00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:57.080
<i>Good. Keep throwing him off!</i>

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:01.910
Stop teasing me, boy.

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:11.590
He bounced!

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:15.180
<i>Adam hit Imai with</i>
<i>the full force of his strength.</i>

00:16:15.260 --> 00:16:20.480
<i>Imai was slammed to the ground</i>
<i>so hard that he bounced!</i>

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:27.860
<i>That was one hell of a blow.</i>
<i>I couldn't protect myself.</i>

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:31.860
-Imai. Can you keep fighting?
-<i>I have to recover quickly.</i>

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:34.610
<i>I need to get back on...</i>

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:43.790
Imai's been blown away again!

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:48.290
<i>He jumped back to reduce the damage.</i>

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:50.050
<i>Wait. When did you get the microphone?</i>

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:55.840
<i>Don't underestimate me!</i>

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:04.060
<i>I can't back off or I'll lose.</i>
<i>All I can do is keep attacking.</i>

00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:10.440
<i>Look at you now, Imai.</i>

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:15.990
<i>Adam's taken down plenty of</i>
<i>heavyweight fighters back in the U.S.</i>

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:20.080
<i>So easy to take wimps down.</i>

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:26.710
<i>I was going to recruit Punk Abbot</i>
<i>to be our fighter.</i>

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:31.500
<i>He had kengan match experience too.</i>

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:34.880
<i>But I met a man</i>
<i>with such incredible physical ability</i>

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:37.090
<i>that he was a lethal killing machine.</i>

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:40.100
<i>That man was Adam Dudley.</i>

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:44.390
<i>On top of that, your physical specs</i>
<i>can't even compare to Adam’s.</i>

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:47.400
<i>No matter how good your technique is,</i>

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:51.400
<i>Adam is capable of turning</i>
<i>the tables with a single blow.</i>

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:56.820
<i>You're just a piece of paper to Adam.</i>

00:17:57.240 --> 00:18:01.370
<i>He's a rock that beats</i>
<i>the shit out of paper.</i>

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:15.970
<i>Crap. He's tougher than I expected.</i>

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:20.300
<i>If this match lasts much longer,</i>
<i>I'll be at a disadvantage.</i>

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:29.150
<i>I'll show you... what I'm capable of.</i>

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:36.150
<i>Look at Imai. He's adopted a low stance.</i>

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:40.660
Wow. Ready to die, boy?

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:43.330
I'll play along.

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:46.160
<i>Adam has changed his stance, too.</i>

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:51.830
It looks like they're both determined
to end this match with their next strike.

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:53.210
<i>I see.</i>

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:11.190
They're moving.

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:15.440
<i>High-Stick Shot.</i>

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:17.440
<i>Zone Activated.</i>

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:28.700
<i>He's done it!</i>
<i>He's been taken down!</i>

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:35.540
<i>He's been hit by cruel reality.</i>

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:41.880
<i>Even a miraculous technique is useless</i>
<i>in the face of overwhelming power.</i>

00:19:46.890 --> 00:19:50.020
This is a perfect sandbag for me.

00:19:51.060 --> 00:19:54.020
What's the matter, kid? Fight back!

00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:56.230
-The best is yet to come!
-That's enough.

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:00.820
Come on, referee. You can't stop me now.

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:05.490
That's enough.

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:09.250
What the hell is happening?

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:12.460
<i>Adam Dudley didn't understand it...</i>

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:15.580
<i>until he saw it.</i>

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:22.630
<i>No shit.</i>

00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:24.930
<i>That's...</i>

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:27.720
<i>That's me.</i>

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:30.600
<i>He's down!</i>

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:33.940
<i>Imai executed a perfect Triangle Choke!</i>

00:20:34.150 --> 00:20:37.610
<i>The King of Stranglers, Cosmo Imai,</i>

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:41.070
<i>showed his pride</i>
<i>in being a jujitsu master.</i>

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:44.240
That was an awesome way to end it.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:49.580
Yeah. Adam probably hasn't even
realized yet that he was attacked.

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:53.960
<i>"Zone" is such a tricky technique.</i>

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:56.330
<i>What is zone?</i>

00:20:57.080 --> 00:20:59.840
<i>It's the technique of discerning</i>
<i>the interval of less than 0.1 second</i>

00:21:00.250 --> 00:21:02.800
<i>when the opponent is focused</i>
<i>exclusively on his attack,</i>

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:05.760
<i>and sneaking into the blind spot</i>
<i>of their conscious mind.</i>

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:10.600
<i>As a result, Cosmo managed to</i>
<i>disappear from his opponent's sight.</i>

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:14.140
<i>Adam probably didn't even realize</i>

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:20.150
<i>that his perception and reality</i>
<i>had gone in opposite directions.</i>

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:23.360
<i>When Adam was caught unawares,</i>

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:25.740
<i>Cosmo instantly moved into</i>
<i>a Triangle Choke.</i>

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:28.870
<i>The whole process took</i>
<i>a fraction of a second.</i>

00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:31.160
Hey, Wakatsuki.

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:34.160
Do you think you can pull that off, too?

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:39.130
No. Imai's the only one
who can fight that way.

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:42.800
The winner is Cosmo Imai.

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:46.840
Cosmo Imai. He's definitely a prodigy.

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:52.600
Oh no. We lost!

00:21:58.770 --> 00:22:04.030
-Imai, well done!
-You're the best, Cosmo!

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:07.360
Nice work, Cos.
I guess it was a narrow win.

00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:09.740
Once you get some rest,
let's go out to eat...

00:22:12.410 --> 00:22:13.370
Cos!

00:22:17.710 --> 00:22:20.380
<i>I've never seen him</i>
<i>so badly injured after a fight.</i>

00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:23.170
<i>This tournament...</i>

00:22:24.260 --> 00:22:26.840
<i>is on a higher level than I imagined.</i>

00:24:05.940 --> 00:24:06.860
PREVIEW

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:09.110
<i>The battle of a hermit versus a riot cop.</i>

00:24:09.360 --> 00:24:11.570
<i>Which one is going to win,</i>

00:24:11.820 --> 00:24:15.280
<i>the unstoppable spear or</i>
<i>the unbreakable shield?</i>

00:24:15.370 --> 00:24:18.200
<i>The greatest mystery in human</i>
<i>history is about to be solved.</i>

00:24:18.330 --> 00:24:19.410
<i>Next episode: "Justice."</i>

00:24:19.500 --> 00:24:20.870
Subtitle translation by
Miki Miyaji
